# Task 1 - Problem Structure and Data Representation (4 marks)
#
# Learning-task decomposition (Mitchell's T, P, E):
# - Task T: Multi-class classification f: R^4096 -> {1, ..., K}
#   * How it constrains the solution: Needs a probabilistic output over K classes -> softmax / cross-entropy (Task 3, 8)
# - Input x: 64x64 grayscale leaf photo, x in [0,1]^4096
#   * How it constrains the solution: High-dimensional, spatially correlated -> redundancy (Task 2), curse of dimensionality (Task 11)
# - Output y: Class label y in {0..K-1}, one-hot e_y in {0,1}^K
#   * How it constrains the solution: Imbalanced classes -> accuracy alone misleading
# - Performance P: Accuracy + macro precision/recall/F1 + confusion matrix
#   * How it constrains the solution: Macro-F1 weights rare diseases equally; recall matters (a missed disease spreads)
# - Experience E: Labelled PlantVillage images
#   * How it constrains the solution: Lab images, uniform background -> optimistic vs field photos
#
# Tensor organisation:
# - one label y_i: scalar, () -> integer class index; one-hot vector (K,) for cross-entropy
# - one image: matrix -> vector, (64,64) -> (4096,) -> flattening discards 2-D neighbourhood
# - mini-batch: matrix / 4-D tensor, (32,4096) or (32,64,64,1) -> rows = samples, enables XW in one matmul
# - dataset: design matrix, (N,4096) -> X^T X is 4096x4096 -> PCA cost
# - labels: vector / matrix, (N,) or (N,K) -> P - Y appears in the gradient (Task 8)
#
# Norms (for x in R^n):
#     ||x||_1 = sum_i |x_i|,   ||x||_2 = sqrt(sum_i x_i^2),   ||x||_inf = max_i |x_i|
# ==============================================================================

